      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While leafy greens are incredibly nutritious, you should be cautious when increasing your intake of certain vegetables like spinach and kale while on warfarin. These greens contain Vitamin K, which can interfere with how warfarin works and potentially affect your blood clotting. It is crucial that you discuss any significant changes to your diet with your doctor or pharmacist to ensure your INR levels remain stable and safe.",
